          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto (third section of join): T-S NS 329.820r + T-S AS 74.141v",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>&ldquo;And what is her profession?&rdquo; He said: &ldquo;She plaits the hair</li>\n<li>of women.&rdquo;&nbsp;They said: &ldquo;Your mother&rsquo;s husband&mdash;what</li>\n<li>is his name?&rdquo; He said to them &ldquo;Yoesph [sic] ben Pappos is his name.&rdquo;</li>\n<li>&ldquo;And what is his profession?&rdquo; He said: &ldquo;He is a carpenter man.&rdquo;&nbsp;&ldquo;And you&mdash;</li>\n<li>what is your name?&rdquo; He said: &ldquo;Y[esh]u.&rdquo; &ldquo;[And] what is your profession?&rdquo;</li>\n<li>He said: &ldquo;I am a hunter.&rdquo;&nbsp;They said to him: &ldquo;These</li>\n<li>writings of the magicians that were found in your hand&mdash;</li>\n<li>are they new or old?&rdquo; He said to them:</li>\n<li>&ldquo;They are old, (belonging to) Balaam son of Peor, and I found them</li>\n<li>in Egypt.&rdquo; They said to him: &ldquo;How do they benefit you?&rdquo;</li>\n<li>He said&nbsp; to them: &ldquo;These (books)&mdash; everything that we want</li>\n<li>to do with them, in everything, we do</li>\n<li>[ ... ] for illnesses [ ... ]</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
